    return (x2 - x1) * (y2 - y1)

What arguments matter are the x and y coordinates of the two corners, and they line up one-to-one with the four unpacked variables. The specification guarantees that the left x is not greater than the right one and the lower y is not greater than the upper one, so the differences are non-negative or zero. When all four coordinates are equal, both differences vanish and the product is zero, as in the third example. The expression has no branches, so it treats integers and floats identically.

The first example spans four in the x direction and three in the y direction, which gives twelve, and the second spans five on both axes, which gives twenty-five, matching the expected values. When the rectangle is a single point at 10, the area is also zero.

Verdict: Correct.

