My approach follows a depth-first search. From the starting cell, I examine the cell to the north, south, west and east, skipping any cell that lies outside the grid or that no longer holds the original value, and recursing into each accepted cell in turn. Whenever I visit a cell, I create a fresh inner list of that row, so each row has a separate identity from the row in the original grid. At the first cell, I change the value to the new one. Neighbours are determined only by their current contents, which means the new value never spreads past the boundary of the region.

