As an input with all of the edge behaviour, I considered the commands N and E with an initial fuel of one. The first move wins and takes the robot to the point one unit north; each step costs one unit, so fuel reaches zero. The next move has no fuel and is skipped, leaving the robot at that same position with zero fuel left. The function returns it together with a remaining fuel of zero, which is the correct result.

